.TH SDL_IN_BYTECAP 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_IN_BYTECAP \- Macro that annotates function params with input buffer size.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_IN_BYTECAP(x) _In_bytecount_(x)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If we were to annotate
.BR memcpy :

.IP
.EX
void *memcpy(void *dst, SDL_IN_BYTECAP(len) const void *src, size_t len);
.EE
.PP

This notes that
.BR src
should be
.BR len
bytes in size and is only read by the function\[char46] The compiler or other analysis tools can warn when this doesn\(aqt appear to be the case\[char46]
.PP
On compilers without this annotation mechanism, this is defined to nothing\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

